+# Vendored crates
+
+## rig-core 0.44.0
+
+Source: crates.io `rig-core` 0.44.0 (MIT, `rig-core/LICENSE`), copied unmodified
+except one line of `rig-core/Cargo.toml`: its `serde_json` dependency no longer
+enables `float_roundtrip`. The workspace uses it through `[patch.crates-io]`.
+
+Why: Cargo unifies features across the build, so `float_roundtrip` would change
+how every serde_json float in the runtime parses. JEV request bodies re-serialize
+capsule state through serde_json, so last-digit float changes alter request
+bytes; recorded exchanges are keyed by request SHA-256 and stopped replaying
+(measured on the DecisionBench fixture: 8 of 222 recorded answers lost). Rig's
+`preserve_order` stays (Rig needs IndexMap APIs); OXIDE writers that must be
+byte-stable sort object keys explicitly (`sort_all_objects`).
+
+Upgrading: copy the new release from crates.io, re-apply the one-line change,
+then run `mise run verify` (the frozen-baseline and DecisionBench tests cover
+the behaviour this patch protects). Drop this vendor copy once upstream stops
+requiring `float_roundtrip`.
